{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_02d9da2733c86829e87cc7080c0cd80385247c72e6bf944dc3f7bb6018e0ad94"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A shared GITHUB_TOKEN environment variable serves all agencies, which the README flags as fine for self-hosting but risky in multi-tenant deployments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1dde9a2368f1beb7510213e37e0f9d8bde2ce9755ad64c3ea60710c00727a422"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per-agency repository configuration stores the repo slug in notes and the GitHub token in agent config, with tokens stored encrypted via the Crustocean API."},{"claim_ids":["clm_22bf483f5e359695410926ee93ed2d6a963f98ae1565a09993a203c52b17e08d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Conch is MIT-licensed and positioned as a self-contained reference implementation for building Crustocean agents with Claude tool calling."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2a49d4e50d28edaafa94c69ec380050254282f52ed9caa94eaef716f36ebb978"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Staged writes are held in an in-memory Map and only reach GitHub when commit() runs during PR creation, making changes ephemeral per run."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2e06ab779039c0b68e3e3565350c5808de5534f0f436ff0a0e3b196b11feb390"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Commits are made atomically via the Git Data API (blobs, tree, commit, ref update), avoiding merge conflicts from concurrent contents API calls."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3581b5a0e665b1de8e1d326bf0ef29be000c1eaf54c89e9f35444f662eaab048"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Runs surface in the Crustocean UI as an Agent Run with tool cards, status updates, permission gates, streaming responses, and a collapsible run timeline."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3a46946182127649dc20e6efb8030841b4eadf78b18021a4327ed2cd9d751948"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Branch deletion is hard-blocked for main, master, and the repository's default branch."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57c47dab4c5aa8a9bb8770fef222282e461c11d9870f16c7e296320992a54e93"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The codebase includes index.js for orchestration, lib/ modules for the Anthropic client, tools, repo config, diffs, and a demo workspace, plus workspace/ GitHub helpers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_59ca6517d74d208d2c588fe6ed5cd16d3272e88470138a9710e69c3f49b0ce48"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requires Node.js >= 18, an Anthropic API key, a GitHub token with repo scope, and the @crustocean/sdk, which handles agent lifecycle and is the only external Crustocean dependency."},{"claim_ids":["clm_821eea645d57f526532c1b1e71d28adf122c2c3afaffb120048f13c1e1512fed"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent can read and explore files, search code, write targeted patches, create and manage pull requests (merge, comment, inspect checks), and delete merged feature branches."},{"claim_ids":["clm_86a0c9b935eb2e1de33284e6b33d98f0dd98d9c361ea897c0fd65c3a733696b5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Chat commands include !conch connect owner/repo, disconnect, status, and help; users can also @mention Conch with coding tasks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d95280e3619c8fc9c1aa8cb45bd48a92d2a442514aa84b5a025f513a201c3da"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"File path validation rejects directory traversal, null bytes, and absolute paths, and writes are capped at 2 MB to prevent memory exhaustion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9ecca8900d39e33acc284fe09364058a3a3e402ab9247ce1ffc09e23d1855342"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Conch is a stateless worker with no database, filesystem, or ports, connecting to Crustocean via WebSocket and GitHub via REST; deployable via Railway, Docker, or any Node.js host."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a1c21d538d7a0bb0c749246497284ed96202bd20dd18f1bc74871a0f3c33afaa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"create_pull_request, merge_pull_request, and delete_branch are permission-gated and require explicit user approval in the Crustocean UI before executing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b58d468344c0372116dff28b529d16f794c89c4c13e505f470ba231a7dba66d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Conch is a cloud coding agent powered by Claude that reads repositories, writes patches, and opens pull requests, steered from Crustocean chat."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ecaf7a779ad00825b0d8f5c91a6ceef68d47b6fdf89c13abff4d3d8a8ad15760"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the private @crustocean/sdk can be made available via npm link, a file: workspace reference in package.json, or publishing to a private registry."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f58b82979bce836a3f9e1cd681735f23c8297a60c00fad802a5ef2131372a23c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: setup involves creating the agent via /agency and /boot commands, copying .env.example to .env with API URL, agent token, and Anthropic key, then npm install and npm start."}],"claim_ids":["clm_02d9da2733c86829e87cc7080c0cd80385247c72e6bf944dc3f7bb6018e0ad94","clm_1dde9a2368f1beb7510213e37e0f9d8bde2ce9755ad64c3ea60710c00727a422","clm_22bf483f5e359695410926ee93ed2d6a963f98ae1565a09993a203c52b17e08d","clm_2a49d4e50d28edaafa94c69ec380050254282f52ed9caa94eaef716f36ebb978","clm_2e06ab779039c0b68e3e3565350c5808de5534f0f436ff0a0e3b196b11feb390","clm_3581b5a0e665b1de8e1d326bf0ef29be000c1eaf54c89e9f35444f662eaab048","clm_3a46946182127649dc20e6efb8030841b4eadf78b18021a4327ed2cd9d751948","clm_57c47dab4c5aa8a9bb8770fef222282e461c11d9870f16c7e296320992a54e93","clm_59ca6517d74d208d2c588fe6ed5cd16d3272e88470138a9710e69c3f49b0ce48","clm_821eea645d57f526532c1b1e71d28adf122c2c3afaffb120048f13c1e1512fed","clm_86a0c9b935eb2e1de33284e6b33d98f0dd98d9c361ea897c0fd65c3a733696b5","clm_9d95280e3619c8fc9c1aa8cb45bd48a92d2a442514aa84b5a025f513a201c3da","clm_9ecca8900d39e33acc284fe09364058a3a3e402ab9247ce1ffc09e23d1855342","clm_a1c21d538d7a0bb0c749246497284ed96202bd20dd18f1bc74871a0f3c33afaa","clm_b58d468344c0372116dff28b529d16f794c89c4c13e505f470ba231a7dba66d6","clm_ecaf7a779ad00825b0d8f5c91a6ceef68d47b6fdf89c13abff4d3d8a8ad15760","clm_f58b82979bce836a3f9e1cd681735f23c8297a60c00fad802a5ef2131372a23c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:11Z","created_by_operation":